        "x0": 0.5096999436619718,
        "y0": 0.18657985281241393,
        "x1": 0.9145466334647882,
        "y1": 0.19731162338386507
      },
      "text": "PERRONENDERE. A pardoner. Heame.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5092950985915493,
        "y0": 0.1999135997089656,
        "x1": 0.9408567049014085,
        "y1": 0.22463299914149448
      },
      "text": "PERRY-DANCERS. The aurora borealis. East PERRYE. (1) A squall.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.530347042253521,
        "y0": 0.22826595775310352,
        "x1": 0.9404534792112677,
        "y1": 0.2712920977863057
      },
      "text": "It happened Harold his sonne to arrive at Pountiou against his will, by occasion of a sudden perry, or contrarie winde, that arose while he was on seaboorde. Lambnrde's Perambulation, 1596, p. 357,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5080805633802816,
        "y0": 0.2742681527048276,
        "x1": 0.7679975761126759,
        "y1": 0.28484672327942545
      },
      "text": "(2) A httle cur dog. North.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5076757183098591,
        "y0": 0.2904341747737932,
        "x1": 0.8655644283943655,
        "y1": 0.32098245728940084
      },
      "text": "Precious stones ; jewels. {A.-N.) And alle was set with perrye, Ther was never no better in Crystyant^.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7129321690140844,
        "y0": 0.3257610909627587,
        "x1": 0.933569493633803,
        "y1": 0.3336424992931616
      },
      "text": "MS. Cantab. Ft. U.a8,f. 242",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.506056338028169,
        "y0": 0.3380113080000001,
        "x1": 0.6708218041690139,
        "y1": 0.3478056369208619
      },
      "text": "PERS. (1) Persia.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5651637183098591,
        "y0": 0.3501294959158622,
        "x1": 0.8513859443380282,
        "y1": 0.37024674974836475
      },
      "text": "We woot bothe bi story and vers That the kyndam of Grace and Pera",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5647588732394366,
        "y0": 0.37490498529103455,
        "x1": 0.8262847402816901,
        "y1": 0.3822277176673385
      },
      "text": "Were hede kyngus in forme tide.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.581762366197183,
        "y0": 0.38766228613517245,
        "x1": 0.935998564056338,
        "y1": 0.39452560754490223
      },
      "text": "Curso)- Mundi, MS. Coll. Trin. Cantab, f. 132.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5056514929577464,
        "y0": 0.3999917920096553,
        "x1": 0.6283227880563379,
        "y1": 0.4087432750035634
      },
      "text": "(2) Company.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.602814309859155,
        "y0": 0.41272698970896565,
        "x1": 0.797944775661972,
        "y1": 0.4316559899268089
      },
      "text": "Al we wite it thi defaut. So siggeth al our pera.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7384374084507042,
        "y0": 0.4372447593889656,
        "x1": 0.9339775774647886,
        "y1": 0.4434589887891037
      },
      "text": "Arthour and Merlin, p. 9.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5044369577464788,
        "y0": 0.44970368760137935,
        "x1": 0.9343791837746479,
        "y1": 0.47047260821473175
      },
      "text": "(3) Sky, or blueish gray colour. There was a kind of cloth so called.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5032224225352112,
        "y0": 0.47450465506344824,
        "x1": 0.8137385915492956,
        "y1": 0.4840113297240348
      },
      "text": "PERSAUNT. Piercing. {A.-N.)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5420875492957745,
        "y0": 0.4884360937931035,
        "x1": 0.9076610285070426,
        "y1": 0.5193677539194124
      },
      "text": "That of the stremis every maner wy3te Astonied was, they weren so bryjte and shene. Ant to the ye for peraaunt for to sene.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6598974647887323,
        "y0": 0.5245525234124139,
        "x1": 0.9331654582535212,
        "y1": 0.5318996184914907
      },
      "text": "Lydgate, MS. Sue. Antiq. 134, f. 23.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.620222647887324,
        "y0": 0.5387228644289656,
        "x1": 0.81495960428169,
        "y1": 0.5453930244095675
      },
      "text": "For thy perseynt charit^.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5020078873239436,
        "y0": 0.5512128758082759,
        "x1": 0.9335694936338028,
        "y1": 0.5845283880587687
      },
      "text": "Gowei; MS. Soc. Antiq. 134, f. 109. PERSCRUTE. To search through. {Lat.) Used by Andrew Borde, Brit. Bibl. iv. 24.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.501603042253521,
        "y0": 0.589382048275862,
        "x1": 0.7619127547042254,
        "y1": 0.6115052050399409
      },
      "text": "PERSE. Equality. (A.-N.) PERSEL. Parsley. Pegge.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5011981971830985,
        "y0": 0.6159277616703448,
        "x1": 0.827503323943662,
        "y1": 0.6252533559777425
      },
      "text": "PERSEVER. To persevere. Shak.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5206307605633802,
        "y0": 0.6311649213793104,
        "x1": 0.878112196507042,
        "y1": 0.662178309233678
      },
      "text": "Whether a daw sit, or whether a daw fly. Whether a daw stand, or whether a daw lye. Whether a daw crecpe, or whether a daw cry,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5210356056338028,
        "y0": 0.66779122,
        "x1": 0.7963294438309858,
        "y1": 0.6738818956932185
      },
      "text": "In what case soever a daw persever,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5202259154929577,
        "y0": 0.6778441862068966,
        "x1": 0.8424866400000001,
        "y1": 0.686545151482923
      },
      "text": "A daw is a daw, and a daw shall be ever.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5007933521126761,
        "y0": 0.6926166644648276,
        "x1": 0.9331662679436619,
        "y1": 0.7654333002716364
      },
      "text": "Tarlton'a Jeats, 1611. PERSIAN-WHEEL. An engine invented to raise a quantity of water sufficient for overflowing lands, that border in the banks of rivers, where the streams lie so low, as to be incapable of doing it.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5003885070422535,
        "y0": 0.7703333238468966,
        "x1": 0.8404551274366197,
        "y1": 0.7930274047063538
      },
      "text": "PERSON. A mask, or actor. {Lat.) PERSONABLE. Personally visible.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5198210704225351,
        "y0": 0.7962740602910345,
        "x1": 0.9303372105915495,
        "y1": 0.8281367737017203
      },
      "text": "My saied lorde of Winchester saied unto the kyng that the kyng his father, so visited with sitkenesse, was not personable. Hall, Henry VI. f. 13.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4999836619718309,
        "y0": 0.8347913820689655,
        "x1": 0.9311452813521126,
        "y1": 0.857234193220762
      },
      "text": "PERSONE. A man. Generally, a man of dignity, a parson or rector of a church.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4999836619718309,
        "y0": 0.8617856009806897,
        "x1": 0.7684056599436613,
        "y1": 0.8719361470717022
      },
      "text": "PERSORE. A piercing-iron.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5781187605633803,
        "y0": 0.8785575812606897,
        "x1": 0.841268866028169,
        "y1": 0.9323495679553446
      },
      "text": "3e, je, seyd the persore. That at I sey it shall be sure Whi chyd je iche one with other ? Wote 56 wele I ame jour brother ! Therefore none contrary me.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5797381408450704,
        "y0": 0.9371741747737931,
        "x1": 0.9299291267605633,
        "y1": 0.9445442645880117
      },
      "text": "Fore as I sey so schall it be. MS.Ashmole Cl>",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
  ],
